                <pb facs="0205" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg198"/>

                <head>No. 125.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs states war vessel not ordered Bluefields and British
                    notification to Nicaraguau commissioner merely caveat pending discussion, and
                    not intended as conclusive. Dispatches now on way explain situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
